# fresh_res_reserve_odd_entries: TaskCore::rebuild_task's ResourceManager::reserve_objects over entry kinds no other scenario puts in a placement task: a type 3 (mipmapped texture) and a type 9 (serializer texture) entry, with zero placements, reach their case labels and reserve nothing; a type 7 entry whose record is 4 bytes, with a nonzero placement, goes to ResourceManager::reserve_object, whose header read fails, and reserves nothing either. None of the records is ever made: an exec with no command buffers maps the lists (and so runs reserve_objects), and completes, and a fill of a buffer B runs. The placement entries of the three are unchanged. Isolate only: in process no task has argument buffers, so a placement list is never read.
